  "_id": "KZHhXmjfOQ0cETge",
  "name": "Mass Polymorph",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "icons/creatures/mammals/goat-horned-blue.webp",
  "folder": "lepc438ersrWtxJR",
  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You try to transform any number of creatures in a 30-foot Emanation originating from you into identical Beasts. Each creature in the Emanation must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or shape-shift into a Beast form for the duration. A creature that isn’t a Beast, a Giant, a Humanoid, or a Monstrosity succeeds automatically.</p><p>The new form can be any Beast of your choice with a Challenge Rating of 0 (a @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.actors24.Actor.mmGoat0000000000]{Goat} is recommended). Each target’s game statistics are replaced by the stat block of that Beast, but it keeps its alignment, personality, creature type, Hit Points, and Hit Point Dice.</p><p>Each target gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the Hit Points of the Beast form, and the spell ends early on a target that has no Temporary Hit Points left.</p><p>The targets are limited in the actions they can perform by the anatomy of their new form, and they can’t speak or cast spells. Each target’s gear melds into the new form, and the creature can’t use or otherwise benefit from any of it.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-ywIpFeAt44H5Hz42\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Transform the creatures that fail by hand (or with Foundry’s transformation), and give them the Temporary Hit Points.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
